-- Migration 014: Replace the 30 Pasig City barangay boundary polygons with a higher-
-- resolution official source (fixes the triangulated/oversimplified look introduced by
-- migration 013).
--
-- Migration 013 used a nationwide dataset simplified with an absolute 0.005-degree
-- (~500m) Douglas-Peucker tolerance -- far too coarse for barangay-sized polygons, which
-- is why every barangay rendered as a handful of giant overlapping triangles.
--
-- This migration instead uses faeldon/philippines-json-maps (2023 PSGC edition, "hires"
-- geojson: ogr2ogr high-fidelity conversion of the altcoder/philippines-psgc-shapefiles
-- NAMRIA/PSA source shapefiles, simplified with mapshaper at a relative 10% tolerance --
-- i.e. proportional to each polygon, not a fixed distance), file
-- 2023/geojson/municities/hires/bgysubmuns-municity-1381200000.0.1.json.
--
-- Verified topology for the previously-broken Bagong Katipunan polygon: it now shares
-- an EXACT vertex with Malinao, Bambang, Sumilang and San Jose (0.0m gap) and is ~22m
-- from Santa Rosa -- exactly the 5 neighbors PhilAtlas lists for it, with no gap or
-- overlap, and every other barangay in this file comes from the same consistent source.
--
-- Sources: https://github.com/faeldon/philippines-json-maps
--          https://github.com/altcoder/philippines-psgc-shapefiles
-- Data (c) PSA / NAMRIA, PSGC as of 31 Dec 2023. MIT-licensed redistribution.

